  "prompt": "Fleur, who runs trade marketing, is planning next year's promotion calendar and asks how much margin each 2025 promotion made. Return one row for every promotion with a start_date from 2025-01-01 to 2025-12-31, both days included, including a promotion that no order line carried, which then has 0 for revenue_eur and margin_eur. Return six columns, in this order: promo_code; promo_type; discount_pct; n_products, the number of products the promotion covers, whether or not they sold; revenue_eur, the net revenue of all order lines that carry the promotion, where a line's net revenue is quantity times unit_price_eur minus line_discount_eur; and margin_eur, the gross margin of those same lines, where a line's gross margin is its net revenue minus quantity times the product's unit_cost_eur. Each order line counts once. Do not round. Sort by discount_pct from highest to lowest; when promotions share a discount_pct, sort them by promo_code from A to Z.",
